---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Container from '../components/Container.astro';
import PolicyArticle from '../components/PolicyArticle.astro';
import SiteCta from '../components/SiteCta.astro';
import TextLink from '../components/TextLink.astro';
import { withBase } from '../data/site';
import { policyLastUpdated } from '../data/policies';
import { hasContactFormEndpoint, hasPublicCalUrl } from '../data/integrations';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Accessibility | She Who Remembers"
  description="Accessibility intent for the She Who Remembers website, current practices, known limits, and how to report an access problem."
>
  <Hero
    heading="Accessibility"
    lede="The site should be usable. If it is not, there is a way to say so."
    surface="light"
    spacing="compact"
  >
    <p>
      This statement describes intent and current practice. It is not a certification, an audit
      report, or a claim of perfect access.
    </p>
  </Hero>

  <Section surface="light" spacing="compact">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <PolicyArticle lastUpdated={policyLastUpdated}>
        <h2>Commitment</h2>
        <p>
          She Who Remembers aims to follow recognized accessibility practices so visitors can read,
          move, and take the next step without being locked out by the interface. The work is
          ongoing. This page will be updated as the site changes.
        </p>

        <h2>Current accessibility practices</h2>
        <p>The public site currently includes:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>semantic page landmarks, including a main content region</li>
          <li>a skip link to the main content</li>
          <li>keyboard-accessible site navigation</li>
          <li>visible focus states</li>
          <li>native form controls with labels, when the contact form is shown</li>
          <li>native details and summary elements for FAQ answers</li>
          <li>reduced-motion support for visitors who request it</li>
          <li>responsive layouts across common screen sizes</li>
          <li>a contrast-conscious palette</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Photography is not yet used as public content. When images are added, they will include
          text alternatives. Decorative marks are hidden from assistive technology where they do
          not add meaning.
        </p>

        <h2>Keyboard access</h2>
        <p>
          Primary navigation, text links, buttons, and FAQ summaries are meant to be reachable
          from the keyboard. FAQ items use native details elements, so more than one answer can
          remain open. Focus is indicated with a visible ring, not by color change alone.
        </p>

        <h2>Color and contrast</h2>
        <p>
          The palette is chosen to keep body text readable on the cream and indigo surfaces used
          throughout the site. Color is not the only way status is communicated. This is not a
          claim of a formal contrast audit or a WCAG certificate.
        </p>

        <h2>Responsive design</h2>
        <p>
          Layouts are built to wrap on small screens. Long headings, lists, and calls to action
          are allowed to break rather than force horizontal scrolling. Line length for reading is
          held to a readable measure.
        </p>

        <h2>Motion</h2>
        <p>
          If your system requests reduced motion, the site shortens or removes non-essential
          animation and smooth scrolling. Atmospheric decoration is kept quieter in that case.
        </p>

        <h2>Forms</h2>
        {
          hasContactFormEndpoint ? (
            <p>
              The contact form uses native inputs, a native select, and a native textarea, each
              with a visible label. Required fields are named in the label text. Validation uses
              the browser&apos;s native required and email checks.
            </p>
          ) : (
            <p>
              The contact form is visible as a preview while message submission is not active. In
              that state the fields are disabled, the status is explained in text, and nothing
              can be submitted. When the form is connected, it will use native labeled controls.
            </p>
          )
        }

        <h2>Known limitations</h2>
        <p>
          Some parts of a visit are not fully controlled here. Webfonts are loaded from Google
          Fonts. If that service is slow, blocked, or incompatible with a particular setup, system
          fallback fonts are specified.
        </p>
        <p>
          An internal style-guide is used during local design review. It is not part of the
          public website.
        </p>

        <h2>Third-party services</h2>
        <p>
          Accessibility of external platforms is partly controlled by those providers. This site
          does not claim to control:
        </p>
        <ul>
          {
            hasPublicCalUrl ? (
              <li>the external booking calendar used for scheduling</li>
            ) : (
              <li>a future external booking calendar, once scheduling is connected</li>
            )
          }
          {
            hasContactFormEndpoint ? (
              <li>the external form provider that receives contact messages</li>
            ) : (
              <li>a future static-form provider, once contact delivery is connected</li>
            )
          }
          <li>a future payment processor, if paid offerings are later configured</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          When you leave this site to use one of those tools, their interface, keyboard behavior,
          and alternatives are theirs.
        </p>

        <h2>Accessibility feedback</h2>
        <p>
          If you find a barrier, write through the{' '}
          <TextLink href={withBase('/contact')}>Contact</TextLink> page. Describe the page, what
          you were trying to do, and what got in the way, if you can. You do not need to use
          technical language.
        </p>
        <p>
          There is no separate accessibility email published on this site. A street address is
          not listed because one has not been provided for publication.
        </p>

        <h2>Ongoing improvement</h2>
        <p>
          This statement will be revised when the site adds imagery, live booking, live contact
          delivery, or payment. The date at the top of the article is the last intentional update,
          not a stamp generated by every build.
        </p>
      </PolicyArticle>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <SiteCta
    heading="If something on the site is in the way"
    primary={{ label: 'Contact', href: withBase('/contact') }}
    secondary={{ label: 'Home', href: withBase('/') }}
  >
    <p>Name the page and the barrier. That is enough to start.</p>
  </SiteCta>
</BaseLayout>
